+## Private HTTPS (work in progress)
+
+The optional native Caddy TLS listener accepts `HUB_WEB_SCHEME=https`,
+`HUB_TLS_PORT` (default 8490), `HUB_TLS_CERT_FILE` and `HUB_TLS_KEY_FILE` in
+the host's mise configuration. Obtain a certificate covering the portal, login,
+console and every declared project app before enabling it. Cloudflare DNS-01 can
+issue wildcard certificates while applications remain private on Tailscale.
+
+Forward private TCP 443 to the loopback TLS listener. Preserve the existing
+Tailscale Serve configuration before changing any route. This is TCP forwarding,
+not TLS termination by Tailscale, because the certificate covers your own domain.
+Keep all application DNS records unproxied and pointed at the private Tailscale IP.
+
+The renderer uses secure cookies, HTTPS public links and exact HTTPS origin checks
+in this mode. Configure each project with the same parent domain, the hub's
+`auth_upstream`, and a D62 provider setting `FYSO_WEB_SCHEME=https`.
+Every certificate renewal must reload Caddy. Validate its generated configuration
+before restarting; missing certificate files fail the pre-stop check.
+
+Tests are in `tests/https.test.cjs`. Set `FYSO_TEST_CADDY` and
+`FYSO_TEST_TINYAUTH` to explicit native binaries and `FYSO_TEST_FRAMEWORK_ROOT`
+to a framework checkout to run the complete fixture with `node --test`.
+The fixture uses real Tinyauth/Caddy, three native framework gateways and simulated
+app/console upstreams: one login, secure session cookies, all declared routes,
+cross-origin rejection, cookie stripping and global logout replay rejection.
+It generates self-signed fixture certificates and validates them against an explicit
+test trust anchor. It does not bypass verification for deployed certificates.
+
+This implementation has local fixture coverage, not live issuance or authenticated
+deployment acceptance. Do not treat it as a completed migration.
+
